  "caveats": [
    "Calibrated from ONE known-good sample (this repository at HEAD). The plateau's upper edge is that single sample's score, so the recommended threshold is determined by one data point and is PROVISIONAL. It is a REGRESSION DETECTOR, not an absolute quality bar: eight well-regarded repositories were reviewed at the shipped default (--samples 5) and ONE is clean -- the other seven have 3 to 54 confirmed blocking findings each -- and a ninth (disko) was pre-screened only, so there is no known-good class to calibrate an absolute bar against. The blocking-finding gate is the absolute control. Use this value as the bar for a repository's first run and a regression line thereafter (--baseline auto). See docs/CALIBRATION.md, 'The clean class is empty'.",
    "d* for tools that found nothing on the clean baseline is floored at 0.05 findings/KLOC rather than 0, because d*=0 collapses the Hill curve to a step at the origin. Floored entries are marked; the aggregate curve anchors only on tools with a real baseline reading.",
    "This calibrates the DETERMINISTIC half only. The LLM half is not calibrated here; that needs labelled real council runs, ~9 min each.",
    "Weights (alpha_t) remain the working defaults. \u00a77 says reweight only with evidence, and there is not yet evidence that any dimension's findings track real defects better than another's."
  ]
